The AI must distinguish between:

- Verified facts
- Reasonable interpretations
- Unsupported claims
- Predictions
- Opinions
- Satire
- Ambiguous statements

Do not force a verdict when evidence is insufficient.

A claim can be UNVERIFIED without being FALSE.

## Verdict Output

Every investigation should produce:

- Original submitted content
- Extracted claim
- Verdict
- Plain-language explanation
- Supporting evidence
- Contradicting evidence
- Important context
- Source citations
- Evidence limitations
- Investigation date
- AI-generated analysis disclaimer

Use a confidence or evidence-strength indicator only if it is clearly defined and properly calibrated.

Do not display fake probabilities such as 99.9% truth.

Distinguish:

- Evidence strength
- Source agreement
- Model uncertainty
- Statistical confidence

These are different concepts.

